printk: nbcon: Use raw_cpu_ptr() instead of open coding

jira KERNEL-749
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-611.41.1.el9_7
commit-author John Ogness <john.ogness@linutronix.de>
commit d33d5e683b0d3b4f5fc6a49ce17583f8ca663944
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-611.41.1.el9_7/d33d5e68.failed

There is no need to open code a non-migration-checking
this_cpu_ptr(). That is exactly what raw_cpu_ptr() is.

